===Etymology 2===
[[File:381_Алас_Мамыкан.jpg|right|thumb|An '''alas''', filled by a lake, in [[Yakutia]].]]
{{swp|+ (geography)}}
From {{der|en|sah|алаас}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/əˈlɑːs/|/əˈlæs/}}<!-- |a=US,UK --><!--sometimes also /ˈɑˌlɑs/ -->

====Noun====
{{en-noun|+|alasses}}

# A type of {{l|en|geological}} {{l|en|depression}} formed by the {{l|en|subsidence}} of {{l|en|permafrost}}, sometimes (partially) filled by a [[lake]].
#: {{altform-inline|en|alass|alaas}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1973|title=Arctic Bulletin|page=35
|passage={{...}} '''alasses''' probably exist south of the Yukon Flats. Another bus tour went to the east, and '''alasses''' and pingos were examined on the terraces.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Mary Chapman|title=The Geology of Mars: Evidence from Earth-Based Analogs|page=292
|passage={{...}} '''alasses'''. They are formed when a large quantity of ground ice thaws (up to 80% by volume) in permafrost. '''Alasses''' are characteristics of the thermal degradation stages of permafrost. Their subsequent thaw induces a lowering of the [terrain].}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=Colin K. Ballantyne|title=Periglacial Geomorphology|page=129
|passage={{...}} permafrost (yedoma), the large volume loss that accompanies the melt of excess ice to produce an '''alas''' is irreversible, and secondary thermokarst lakes developed in ice-rich epigenetic permafrost on the '''alas''' floor are likely to be much smaller and shallower than the original thermokarst lake.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=Takeshi Ohta; Tetsuya Hiyama; Yoshihiro Iijima|title=Water-Carbon Dynamics in Eastern Siberia|page=195
|passage={{...}} permafrost underneath has been thawing, due to both the warming climate and shifting hydrological processes. The exact extent of change is highly dependent on the specific context of each '''alas's''' physical characteristics.}}

